From: daveey <daveey@users.noreply.github.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 23:04:11 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] [daveey] let successor code re-evaluate durable wall retries

A wall failure in the pre-retirement skew window books a reset-time close-out. The replay timer dies with its backend, but the successor inherits the durable deadline without the booking code identity. Retirement-only reset distrust cannot repair that earlier booking.

Stamp long failed-wake deferrals with frozen host-loop code SHA and the existing short deadline. Candidate discovery uses the earlier deadline only for a known different build. Keep legacy/unknown/same-code rows, busy retries, CAS and attempt budgets unchanged; no migration or new replay budget.

Proof: regression fails on baseline at successor discovery; 75 tests across successor/notice/superseded suites and 141 tests in all remaining notice-guarantee importer suites pass. Seven source mutants killed; scripts/check passes. Reverse by reverting this commit.
